  "assumptions": [
    "This is a nominal no-opponent scenario, with successful sensing and mechanical transfers unless an explicit simulated failure is supplied.",
    "Initial cube counts are from the rules; their exact slot positions are evenly spaced display assumptions and are not surveyed placements.",
    "Cargo is a bottom-to-top list. Each successful Grap appends one cube on top. Build removes the current top cube at each release. Firmware does not identify cube order, color, pickup success or final placement.",
    "An unload preserves the cargo stack order. A staged load recovers that stack in the same bottom-to-top order. These physical outcomes are assumptions, not sensor observations.",
    "Build adds at most the actually available cargo cubes to an actually existing base. A missing base contributes zero layers; no six-layer structure is created from the Build call alone.",
    "An orange-only base of three cubes plus cargo [purple,orange,orange] produces the nominal layer order [orange,orange,orange,orange,orange,purple] only when all assumed transfers succeed.",
    "Placement x coordinates follow configured lateral offsets and CAD side contact. Placement y=6250 is a display choice, one half cube inside the nominal building platform front edge.",
    "World target placements annotate material destinations. They must not teleport the chassis or alter the production route calibration.",
    "Nominal durations, release timestamps and clearance timestamps are editable simulation inputs, not hardware timings or measured race performance.",
    "Every cube id has one owner. Resource, carried, deposited, building and lost sets must remain disjoint and together contain all 23 initial cube ids.",
    "Carried cubes include cubes held by the arm; arm-to-storage motion changes compartment, not the competition carrying count."
  ],
